        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> After I restart nvim, treesitter does try to install `'c'` and `'cpp`' highlighters but it's stuck in:\n> \n> ```\n> [nvim-treesitter/install/cpp]: Compiling parser\n> ```\n\nIt might take a while to compile a parser. Maybe waiting a bit more will solve this.\nIf not, then I heard that installing `tree-sitter-cli` helps on the `main` branch of tree-sitter. It is [listed as a requirement](https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter/tree/main?tab=readme-ov-file#requirements).\n\n---\n\nClosing as an original issue is resolved.\n\nAlso, to add to the clipboard question. The behavior you experienced with 'kickstart.nvim' is most probably due to [setting `vim.o.clipboard = 'unnamedplus'`](https://github.com/nvim-lua/kickstart.nvim/blob/3338d3920620861f8313a2745fd5d2be39f39534/init.lua#L113-L119). I personally don't like this and prefer to keep Neovim's and system's clipboard separate. But you can adjust this to fit your taste, of course.",
